@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: execute order and cache reuse for proveo build and deploy
' covers: internal/maintain/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/maintain_cmd.go
' covers: defs/lib/docker-build.sh
' covers: defs/**/Dockerfile
' covers: internal/contract/image_build_cache_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/maintain_cmd_test.go
' browser variants layer on the harness ... _spec/defs/browser-layer.puml
' size of that layer ................ _spec/_plans/image-size-reduction.puml
' standing pipeline .......... _spec/internal/maintain/image-build-deploy.puml
' which driver, FROM where ... _spec/_devops/buildx-driver-selection.puml
title Build schedule — bases serial, then a concurrent wave

component "Schedule(ts)" as SCH <<app>>
component "base waves\none target each" as BASES <<app>>
component "harness + sidecar wave\nconcurrent when disjoint" as WAVE <<app>>
component "dependents after parent\n-browser and solidity" as SOL <<app>>
component "elapsed per name\nsummary requires a duration" as ELAP <<app>>
component "type=local mode=max\n--load and --push" as CACHE <<app>>
component "RUN --mount=type=cache\napt · npm · go · pip" as MOUNT <<app>>

SCH ARROW_MAIN BASES
BASES ARROW_MAIN WAVE
WAVE ARROW_MAIN SOL
SCH ARROW_MAIN ELAP
CACHE ARROW_MAIN SCH
MOUNT ARROW_MAIN SCH

note bottom of BASES
  **Bases stay one at a time.** Each
  image is FROM the previous base,
  so a parallel wave would build the
  child before that parent exists.
end note

note bottom of WAVE
  **Registry order is dependency
  order, not execute order.** Harnesses
  with disjoint parents, plus both
  sidecars, share one concurrent wave.
end note

note bottom of CACHE
  **Deploy still rebuilds on push.**
  That build uses the other driver,
  and both modes share one local cache
  so the host architecture can hit.
end note

note bottom of MOUNT
  **A cache mount is not a layer.**
  Apt, npm, Go, and pip keep their
  downloads across a version bump, and
  each image owns its mount id.
end note

@enduml
